{0 tea-melange 0.1.0}

The Elm Architecture in Reason for Melange. Start with the Tea umbrella for
browser applications, or use tea.core, tea.vdom and tea.html independently for
native logic and view tests. tea.test is native-only.

{1 Program lifecycle}

A program initializes a model and commands from flags. Its model-first update
returns the next model and commands. Its pure view produces virtual DOM, and
subscriptions describe active event sources. Every effect returns through the
single message queue. Rendering is batched to animation frames; initialization
renders synchronously.

App.beginner is the unit-returning convenience builder. App.element mounts into
a selected element. App.document owns body contents and title. App.application
also delivers link requests and history changes as messages; the update chooses
whether an internal request should push a URL or an external request should
load a page. Effectful builders return handles whose shutdown operation stops
subscriptions and removes managed event listeners.

{1 Modules}

Html, Attr (also Attributes), Events, Keyed and Svg construct pure views.
Cmd, Sub and Task describe effects. Decode describes portable JSON/event
decoders. Program defines the program record. Http, Url, Navigation, Time,
Random and Animation_frame cover browser effects. Tea.Random combines explicit
seeded generators and the command that obtains a fresh seed.

Runtime.Make takes a Platform.S functor argument. Native tests supply a manual
scheduler instead of linking a browser implementation. Render, Query and
Simulate in tea.test support deterministic native view tests.

{1 Design}

Virtual DOM is the sole renderer. The Elm-style keyed diff and animator are
original Reason implementations of public algorithms, not copied source.
ADR-02's proposed port is superseded by the license audit; no melange-tea or
melange-webapi dependency is included. ADR-06 uses a platform functor rather
than a Dune virtual module. Sources are exclusively Reason, using Dune's
built-in dialect. JSX, server rendering, hydration and persistence are outside
v0.1 scope.
